WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.401 --> 00:00:03.103
-You know our next guest from
NBC's "The Office"

00:00:03.103 --> 00:00:04.737
and "Brooklyn Nine-Nine,"
as well as the films

00:00:04.737 --> 00:00:06.239
"Pineapple Express"
and "This is the End."

00:00:06.239 --> 00:00:09.275
He executive-produced
and stars in "Killing It,"

00:00:09.275 --> 00:00:10.843
which is streaming now
on Peacock.

00:00:10.843 --> 00:00:12.145
Let's take a look.

00:00:13.679 --> 00:00:15.948 line:0%
-Oh, yeah, guess it was, like,

00:00:15.948 --> 00:00:18.183 line:0%
pouring rain
till like one minute ago.

00:00:18.183 --> 00:00:19.819 line:0%
The weather is crazy.

00:00:19.819 --> 00:00:22.321
I don't care what Marco says.
Climate change is real.

00:00:22.321 --> 00:00:24.657
-I believe in climate change.

00:00:24.657 --> 00:00:26.258
-Doesn't take two people to
answer the door, Marco.

00:00:26.258 --> 00:00:28.861
-Were you just, uh,
hiding a bike in our bush?

00:00:28.861 --> 00:00:30.496
-God, seriously?
Why are you so obsessed with me?

00:00:30.496 --> 00:00:33.232
-I am not obsessed with you.
I live here. It's my bush.

00:00:33.232 --> 00:00:34.567
-Now it seems like
you're obsessed with bushes.

00:00:34.567 --> 00:00:36.101
-I am not obsessed with bushes.

00:00:36.101 --> 00:00:37.203
-Yeah, you are, and it's weird,

00:00:37.203 --> 00:00:38.571
because it's not even
your bush, bro.

00:00:38.571 --> 00:00:40.039
-It's in front of my house.
-But you rent.

00:00:40.039 --> 00:00:41.974
You're borrowing that bush.
-Well, at least I have a bush.

00:00:41.974 --> 00:00:42.975
-You're a bush borrower.
-You live in an apartment.

00:00:42.975 --> 00:00:44.778
-You're a bush borrower.

00:00:45.411 --> 00:00:46.979
Bush borrower.

00:00:46.979 --> 00:00:50.450
-Please welcome back to the show
our friend Craig Robinson!

00:00:50.450 --> 00:00:54.521
[ Cheers and applause ]
♪♪

00:01:13.540 --> 00:01:15.374
How are you, buddy?
-I'm good. How you doing?

00:01:15.374 --> 00:01:18.211
-I'm good. You got a backpack?

00:01:18.211 --> 00:01:19.211
-Yeah, yeah.

00:01:19.211 --> 00:01:21.080
It's my "Seth Meyers"

00:01:21.080 --> 00:01:25.117
emotional-support
Teddy-bear knapsack.

00:01:25.117 --> 00:01:26.886
-Wow! That's --
-Yeah.

00:01:26.886 --> 00:01:30.923
-Well, I'm touched.

00:01:30.923 --> 00:01:33.793
-Yeah, you always give
such great gifts and stuff,

00:01:33.793 --> 00:01:35.194
so I never have
anywhere to put it,

00:01:35.194 --> 00:01:36.496
except for the bag you give us.

00:01:36.496 --> 00:01:37.764
-Oh, gotcha.

00:01:37.764 --> 00:01:39.599
So, like, you mean the greenroom
gifts that we give.

00:01:39.599 --> 00:01:41.700
-The greenroom --
Yeah, I got cookies in here.

00:01:41.700 --> 00:01:45.171
-Okay, great.
-I got a card from Seth.

00:01:45.171 --> 00:01:48.073
-Yeah, I wrote a card.
-Y'all want me to read it?

00:01:48.073 --> 00:01:49.609
-Sure.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:01:49.609 --> 00:01:52.745
-I haven't opened it.
Can you see that? "Craig."

00:01:52.745 --> 00:01:53.812
-Yeah, that's --
People are gonna see

00:01:53.812 --> 00:01:55.014
I have weird handwriting.

00:01:55.014 --> 00:01:57.149
-Okay, yeah, yeah, yeah, yeah,
yeah, yeah, yeah.

00:01:57.149 --> 00:01:59.652
Alright, alright, alright.
This wasn't planned, guys.

00:01:59.652 --> 00:02:01.253
-If I'd known
you were doing this,

00:02:01.253 --> 00:02:02.522
I would have
written something longer.

00:02:02.522 --> 00:02:04.424
-Oh. Well, no, that's fine.

00:02:04.424 --> 00:02:08.394
"Craig, so happy
you're here in person."

00:02:08.394 --> 00:02:09.395
-That's right.

00:02:09.395 --> 00:02:10.563
So, that's very lovely,

00:02:10.563 --> 00:02:12.165
'cause the last time
we talked was on Zoom.

00:02:12.165 --> 00:02:13.499
-We were on Zoom.
-Yeah.

00:02:13.499 --> 00:02:15.435
And now here we are in person.
-It was during last year.

00:02:15.435 --> 00:02:16.769
-During last year.

00:02:16.769 --> 00:02:20.439
And now, in that time, you have
shot a new a new comedy.

00:02:20.439 --> 00:02:22.474
-Or the year before last.
-Was it the year before last?

00:02:22.474 --> 00:02:23.843
-Wow!
-It's been a long time.

00:02:23.843 --> 00:02:26.212
-Yeah, it has been a long time.
-So, congratulations.

00:02:26.212 --> 00:02:27.713
This show is great.
It's "Killing It."

00:02:27.713 --> 00:02:29.749
It's some guys that you met on
"Brooklyn Nine-Nine,"

00:02:29.749 --> 00:02:31.050
a show you were great in,
as well.

00:02:31.050 --> 00:02:33.853
-Dan Goor and Luke Del Tredici.

00:02:33.853 --> 00:02:36.188
-Lovely gentlemen.
-Lovely gentlemen.

00:02:36.188 --> 00:02:39.525
-And this is a very, very
different kind of show.

00:02:39.525 --> 00:02:41.260
I mean, these guys --
Obviously, they were involved in

00:02:41.260 --> 00:02:44.864
"Brooklyn Nine-Nine,"
but, tonally, this is different.

00:02:44.864 --> 00:02:48.267
-It's me hunting snakes.

00:02:48.267 --> 00:02:49.635
-Yeah.
-Yeah.

00:02:49.635 --> 00:02:50.969
So it's a little weird.

00:02:50.969 --> 00:02:55.008
I met with Dan and Luke,
and they came with these ideas.

00:02:55.008 --> 00:02:56.442
And it was like three ideas,

00:02:56.442 --> 00:02:58.144
but at the end,
this one just stood out.

00:02:58.144 --> 00:02:59.311
And it's real.

00:02:59.311 --> 00:03:02.348
It's like people
actually are commissioned

00:03:02.348 --> 00:03:06.084
by the government to hunt snakes
because, I guess,

00:03:06.084 --> 00:03:08.687
back in the day, drug dealers
and whoever bought snakes

00:03:08.687 --> 00:03:11.323
as pets, let them loose,
try to be like Scarface,

00:03:11.323 --> 00:03:13.325
you know,
and they sent them out,

00:03:13.325 --> 00:03:15.160
and now Florida
is overrun with snakes.

00:03:15.160 --> 00:03:17.330
-Too many snakes, yeah.
The wrong kind of snakes.

00:03:17.330 --> 00:03:20.699
-'Cause nothing eats the snakes,
but they eat everything.

00:03:20.699 --> 00:03:21.967
-And now, we're you --

00:03:21.967 --> 00:03:23.703
Did you have to get over
a fear of snakes?

00:03:23.703 --> 00:03:25.271
Did you have that before
you did this show?

00:03:25.271 --> 00:03:28.374
-I had a fear of snakes
till about 2015,

00:03:28.374 --> 00:03:32.845
when I went to Australia with
my band, The Nasty Delicious.

00:03:32.845 --> 00:03:34.614
-The Nasty Delicious.

00:03:34.614 --> 00:03:37.951
-And we went to
an animal sanctuary,

00:03:37.951 --> 00:03:39.685
and it was so amazing, Seth.

00:03:39.685 --> 00:03:43.589
We met a cockatoo.
We sang till he started dancing.

00:03:43.589 --> 00:03:47.493
His hair came up, a little Afro.

00:03:47.493 --> 00:03:49.295
We met a koala bear,
and I held it.

00:03:49.295 --> 00:03:51.964
It was the second-best hug
in my life.

00:03:51.964 --> 00:03:53.032
The first was my mother.

00:03:53.032 --> 00:03:54.400
-That's very nice.
That's very sweet.

00:03:54.400 --> 00:03:55.801
-The second was this koala bear.

00:03:55.801 --> 00:03:58.204
It felt like holding
a strong baby.

00:03:58.204 --> 00:04:04.277
And then we met the snakes,
and I was gonna, you know,

00:04:04.277 --> 00:04:05.411
pretend like
I was taking a picture,

00:04:05.411 --> 00:04:06.779
but too scared to touch a snake.

00:04:06.779 --> 00:04:08.147
But then I ended up touching it,

00:04:08.147 --> 00:04:09.949
and it was,
like, amazing-feeling.

00:04:09.949 --> 00:04:11.483
And they put
the snake around my neck,

00:04:11.483 --> 00:04:12.785
and I was like, "Wow.

00:04:12.785 --> 00:04:14.119
The snake means me no harm.

00:04:14.119 --> 00:04:18.124
I've been misled by the Bible
and 'Indiana Jones.'"

00:04:19.459 --> 00:04:24.463
-Have you ever had to
kill pests in real life?

00:04:24.463 --> 00:04:28.367
-I had an ant problem
when I moved into my house.

00:04:28.367 --> 00:04:32.438
Yeah, I didn't know ants
were so many and so organized.

00:04:32.438 --> 00:04:34.607
-Yeah, they are.
-Yeah.

00:04:34.607 --> 00:04:35.875
-People don't talk about
the organization of ants.

00:04:35.875 --> 00:04:37.343
-They don't, they don't.

00:04:37.343 --> 00:04:39.545
And they'll disappear
in a second,

00:04:39.545 --> 00:04:42.882
'cause they know when you're
coming to kill them.

00:04:42.882 --> 00:04:43.983
It's weird.

00:04:43.983 --> 00:04:46.252
-They know
'cause they have a lookout.

00:04:46.252 --> 00:04:48.755
They have a lookout ant --
very famous.

00:04:48.755 --> 00:04:51.056
-Whoo!
-Okay, great.

00:04:51.056 --> 00:04:52.358
-I get a little -- Yeah.

00:04:52.358 --> 00:04:53.792
-You could have put that
in the backpack.

00:04:53.792 --> 00:04:55.261
-Yeah, it was,
but then I was like,

00:04:55.261 --> 00:04:58.598
"Let's put it
where I can get it."

00:04:58.598 --> 00:05:00.733
-So, you learned --
we saw from that clip,

00:05:00.733 --> 00:05:02.235
you learned some ASL for this.

00:05:02.235 --> 00:05:03.236
-Yes.

00:05:03.236 --> 00:05:06.004
-Did you have any base coat

00:05:06.004 --> 00:05:07.539
before you started
doing this show?

00:05:07.539 --> 00:05:10.342
-You know,
when I got my master's degree,

00:05:10.342 --> 00:05:17.349
we learned to sign
the alphabet and numbers.

00:05:17.349 --> 00:05:19.952
-Uh-huh.
-And so I had that base.

00:05:19.952 --> 00:05:21.921
But then this was like
learning actual,

00:05:21.921 --> 00:05:23.355
you know, words or phrases.

00:05:23.355 --> 00:05:27.393
Shout-out to Rick,
my ASL teacher, who --

00:05:27.393 --> 00:05:28.961
I thought it was
gonna be a long process,

00:05:28.961 --> 00:05:30.362
'cause the first day,
I kind of fell asleep

00:05:30.362 --> 00:05:31.697
when he was trying to show me.

00:05:31.697 --> 00:05:35.000
But then, after that, I started
to get a rhythm with it,

00:05:35.000 --> 00:05:37.270
and then I learned for
the scenes.

00:05:37.270 --> 00:05:39.705
I haven't quite learned ASL yet,
but I learned for the scenes.

00:05:39.705 --> 00:05:40.806
-That's great.

00:05:40.806 --> 00:05:42.107
I want to ask about this,
'cause you have

00:05:42.107 --> 00:05:43.809
an animated film coming out
called "The Bad Guys."

00:05:43.809 --> 00:05:45.078
-Mm-hmm.
-I'm very excited about it.

00:05:45.078 --> 00:05:46.712
Now, I got a 6-year-old
and a 4-year-old

00:05:46.712 --> 00:05:47.713
Do you think they will enjoy
"The Bad Guys"?

00:05:47.713 --> 00:05:50.016
And which bad guy are you here?

00:05:50.016 --> 00:05:52.251
-I am Mr. Shark.
-Okay, great.

00:05:52.251 --> 00:05:53.285
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:05:53.285 --> 00:05:54.687
-Yeah, yeah. Yeah, yeah.

00:05:56.756 --> 00:05:59.424
It's being hailed
as Tarantino for kids.

00:05:59.424 --> 00:06:01.260
-Okay, that's good.
-So, yeah, check that out.

00:06:01.260 --> 00:06:02.261
-I've been looking for that.

00:06:02.261 --> 00:06:04.062
I've been looking for that.

00:06:04.062 --> 00:06:06.165
But was it fun to do?

00:06:06.165 --> 00:06:08.101
-It was absolutely a blast.

00:06:08.101 --> 00:06:10.870
I did a lot of prep for it.

00:06:10.870 --> 00:06:13.939
I infiltrated a family of sharks
for about a month and a half.

00:06:13.939 --> 00:06:15.641
-You did?
-Yeah.

00:06:15.641 --> 00:06:16.942
-The suit cost $12 million,

00:06:16.942 --> 00:06:18.711
'cause you got to breathe
underwater, but it was worth it.

00:06:18.711 --> 00:06:20.512
-Yeah.
-It was worth it.

00:06:20.512 --> 00:06:21.714
But, no, it was a blast.

00:06:21.714 --> 00:06:24.751
DreamWorks actually
pitched the show to me.

00:06:24.751 --> 00:06:27.353
I went and sat
in their theater room,

00:06:27.353 --> 00:06:29.255
and they were
showing me the cast

00:06:29.255 --> 00:06:30.556
and what the shark
was gonna look like

00:06:30.556 --> 00:06:32.825
and, you know, some of
the lines from the dialogue.

00:06:32.825 --> 00:06:35.160
And I was like, "Hey,
you had me at 'DreamWorks.'"

00:06:35.160 --> 00:06:36.462
-That's great.
-Yeah, it was dope.

00:06:36.462 --> 00:06:37.563
-You're like, "Why are you
doing this pitch?

00:06:37.563 --> 00:06:39.165
I would have said 'yes'
to anything."

00:06:39.165 --> 00:06:41.834
-Could have
done this on the phone.

00:06:41.834 --> 00:06:43.502
-You mentioned your band,
The Nasty Delicious.

00:06:43.502 --> 00:06:45.338
You going back on tour
any one of these days?

00:06:45.338 --> 00:06:47.272
-You know what?
May 4 at The Troubadour.

00:06:47.272 --> 00:06:48.340
-Really?!
-Yeah.

00:06:48.340 --> 00:06:49.409
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:06:49.409 --> 00:06:50.609
-Are you excited?
How long has it been?

00:06:50.609 --> 00:06:51.877
How long has it been?

00:06:51.877 --> 00:06:55.781
-It's been since New Year's
of -- What year is this?

00:06:55.781 --> 00:06:57.616
-This is '22.
-Of 2020.

00:06:57.616 --> 00:06:58.951
-Wow! So it's been a long time.
-So New Year's of 2020.

00:06:58.951 --> 00:07:00.152
-Alright.

00:07:00.152 --> 00:07:04.323
-So we coming together
like tigers in a cage.

00:07:04.323 --> 00:07:05.824
-Alright. That's great.

00:07:05.824 --> 00:07:07.226
I wish I could be there.

00:07:07.226 --> 00:07:08.694
I can't wait for everybody
who gets to be there.

00:07:08.694 --> 00:07:09.695
Thank you so much
for being here, Craig.

00:07:09.695 --> 00:07:10.729
It's always such a pleasure.

00:07:10.729 --> 00:07:13.832
-My man!
-My man. Craig Robinson!

00:07:13.832 --> 00:07:16.769
All 10 episodes of "Killing It"
are streaming now on Peacock,

00:07:16.769 --> 00:07:19.104
and "The Bad Guys"
opens in theaters April 22nd.

00:07:19.104 --> 00:07:20.206
He's the shark.

